<title>BELGIUM: EU coins may have reduced nickel content.</title>
<headline>EU coins may have reduced nickel content.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union demand for nickel in the bloc's new single currency coins could be lower than in existing coins because of health concerns, according to EU officials.</p>
<p>Urged by Sweden, finance ministers from the 15-nation bloc ordered a high-level experts group on Monday to consider reducing the nickel content of the planned 10 and 20 euro cents coins, which are due to come into circulation in 2002.</p>
<p>One official said Sweden was concerned to protect people who were allergic to nickel.</p>
<p>The experts group -- made up of senior officials from national mints -- had wanted to make the content of euro oins the same as for most existing world currencies in order to facilitate recycling, the official said.</p>
<p>BRUSSELS NEWSROOM: +32 2 287-6830</p>
